L** - Chapter count now correct (9/9)\n   221→- **Partial Success:** Chapter titles still malformed (\"Chapter 2: II\") - needs additional fix for title formatting\n   222→- **Impact on Overall Score:** Structure improved from 3/10 to 5/10 (+0.40 points overall)\n   223→\n   224→### Attempt 2 → Attempt 3, Fix 2: Prevent Family Member Merging (CRITICAL Issue #1) - **FAILED**\n   225→- **Issue:** George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson incorrectly merged into single character \"Wilson\" with aliases including both \"George B. Wilson\", \"George Wilson\" AND \"Myrtle\", \"Myrtle Wilson\"\n   226→- **Root Cause Hypothesis:** The `_validate_merge()` function in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` had checks for family members with different first names but same last name, but these checks were nested too deep in conditional logic and didn't catch all cases\n   227→- **Fix Attempted:** Added two early validation checks in `_validate_merge()` BEFORE other complex logic:\n   228→  1. **Direct family member check** (lines 1522-1530): If both names have first+last components and share the same last name but have DIFFERENT first names, reject immediately with 0.05 confidence\n   229→  2. **Ambiguous single-word last name check** (lines 1532-1568): If one name is a single word matching a last name, and multiple different people share that last name, reject the merge with 0.1 confidence\n   230→- **Modified Files:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1502-1568)\n   231→- **Testing:** Verified with existing unit test `tests/test_character_agent.py::TestGatsbyCharacterExtraction::test_gatsby_distinct_pairs_defined` which specifically checks that George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson are kept as distinct characters\n   232→- **Result:** ✗ **FAILED** - George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson are STILL merged in the output\n   233→- **Unexpected Side Effect:** ✗ James Gatz and Gatsby are now SPLIT into separate characters (new critical error)\n   234→- **Impact on Overall Score:** No improvement (still 2/10 for Character Extraction), and introduced new critical error\n   235→- **Lesson Learned:** The fix did not address the root cause. Need to investigate:\n   236→  1. Is the validation being called for the Wilson merge?\n   237→  2. Is the merge happening in a different part of the pipeline?\n   238→  3. Did the fix over-correct and reject valid same-person merges (like Gatsby/Gatz)?\n   239→\n   240→### Attempt 3 → Attempt 4, Fix 3: Filter Ambiguous Last-Name-Only Entries (CRITICAL Issues #1 and #3)\n   241→- **Issue:** Same issues as Attempt 3:\n   242→  1. George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson still incorrectly merged via \"Wilson\" intermediate\n   243→  2. James Gatz and Gatsby incorrectly split into separate characters\n   244→- **Root Cause Analysis:** The validation logic added in Attempt 3 was correct but insufficient. The problem is that the LLM alias resolution was receiving \"Wilson\" (single word), \"George Wilson\", and \"Myrtle Wilson\" as separate names. The LLM would then suggest merging:\n   245→  - \"Wilson\" <- \"George Wilson\" (seems reasonable if you don't know about Myrtle)\n   246→  - \"Wilson\" <- \"Myrtle Wilson\" (seems reasonable if you don't know about George)\n   247→  - This creates a single \"Wilson\" character with both George and Myrtle as aliases\n   248→- **Fix Implemented:** Pre-filter ambiguous last-name-only entries BEFORE alias resolution\n   249→  - Added `_filter_ambiguous_lastnames()` method (lines 1858-1948) that:\n   250→    1. Identifies single-word names that match the last name of multiple full names with DIFFERENT first names\n   251→    2. Removes these ambiguous names from consideration before LLM alias resolution\n   252→    3. Example: If \"Wilson\", \"George Wilson\", and \"Myrtle Wilson\" exist, remove \"Wilson\" entirely\n   253→  - Called this filter at line 327, right after separating proper names from epithets\n   254→- **Modified Files:**\n   255→  - `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 324-327: added filter call)\n   256→  - `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1858-1948: new `_filter_ambiguous_lastnames()` method)\n   257→- **Testing:** All character extraction tests pass:\n   258→  - `tests/test_character_agent.py` - 12 passed\n   259→  - `tests/test_alias_merging.py` - 12 passed\n   260→- **Expected Results:**\n   261→  - George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson will remain separate characters (fixes CRITICAL #1)\n   262→  - Gatsby and James Gatz should merge correctly because \"Gatsby\" is NOT ambiguous (no other full names with different first names share \"Gatsby\" as last name)\n   263→  - This fix is more robust than attempt 3 because it prevents the problematic merge pattern entirely\n   264→- **Impact on Overall Score:**\n   265→  - If successful: Character Extraction 2 → 10 (+2.0 points), Overall 4.65 → 6.65\n   266→  - Still need to fix narrator issue (+0.60) and other issues to cross 8.0 threshold\n   267→\n   268→## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 3)\n   269→- Analysis completed in 60m 9s\n   270→- **Chapter Detection:** Found 9 chapters (✓ correct count!)\n   271→- **Character Extraction:** 58 characters detected\n   272→- **Character Profiles:** 17 profiles generated, 3 low-confidence\n   273→- **Pronunciation Guide:** 628 words flagged (unchanged from attempt 1 & 2)\n   274→- **Warnings/Errors:**\n   275→  - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many (may be false positive)\n   276→  - StructureAgent: 2 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n   277→  - Failed to parse JSON response for Nick\n   278→  - Low confidence profiles: Daisy (0.00), McKee (0.00), Nick (0.30)\n   279→  - Moral valence classification failed for Tom, Daisy, McKee\n   280→- **Narrator:** Detected \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" (still incorrect - should be Nick Carraway)\n   281→\n   282→## Next Action\n   283→Re-run analysis (PROMPT_analyze.md) to verify that Attempt 4 fix resolves the character merging issues.\n   284→\n   2